# Private store copies and field-measurement bundles. A store copy *is* someone's
# memories, and the field bundles quote them in their .txt audit outputs, so neither
# belongs in git history: what gets committed is the digest and the transcription of
# the aggregate numbers (plan §17). The tarballs live here locally and are ignored.
eval/*.tar.gz
eval/store-*/
eval/field-*/
